  "entry": "E67",
  "article": "A Utah microreactor just powered an Nvidia AI chip live on stage, a first for next-generation nuclear in America, and the two companies used the moment to announce a 30-megawatt AI factory in the desert designed to drink zero local water",
  "gold_statement": "the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah",
  "gold_meaning": {
   "who": "NVIDIA and Valar Atomics",
   "what": "agreement to explore nuclear-powered AI factories; a 30MW waterless AI factory in Utah under study",
   "how_much": "30MW",
   "status": "plan"
  },
  "draws": {
   "A1": [
    "More than 75 of these projects, worth around $130 billion, have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom’s Hardware .",
    "Polling covered in the same reporting has 7 out of 10 Americans saying they don’t want one built anywhere near their home.",
    "So the event a nuclear startup and Nvidia staged in the Utah desert on July 1 was aimed squarely at that mood. Valar Atomics wired a Blackwell -based Nvidia desktop unit to its Ward 250 microreactor, served a website off the electricity, and announced a plan for something much bigger that skips the local water entirely.",
    "Valar says the reactor was running at 37% of its intended output during the show, which founder and CEO Isaiah Taylor put at roughly 100 kilowatts of thermal energy.",
    "The current, Taylor told the crowd in remarks carried by Tom’s Hardware , was at that moment “powering Nvidia’s Blackwell chip, which is currently serving this website.”",
    "Bloomberg noted the output amounted to a tiny amount of electricity, and confirmed the part that matters: it’s the first time a next-generation reactor has produced power to run an AI chip in the US.",
    "The paperwork is the bigger caveat. Ward 250 runs under a Department of Energy authorization, not a Nuclear Regulatory Commission license, and the DOE program it belongs to covers research and demonstration rather than commercial sale.",
    "Valar has also joined Texas and Utah in litigation arguing the NRC lacks licensing authority over some microreactors, according to Reuters.",
    "Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”",
    "On the computing side, Nvidia says its DSX facility design cuts cooling water from roughly 2.6 million gallons per megawatt per year to near zero, with warm-water loops replacing the usual chillers.",
    "Run Nvidia’s own number against a conventional 30 MW site and you land around 78 million gallons a year. The pitch here is zero of it, in a desert.",
    "“Through this work with Valar Atomics, Nvidia is exploring how behind-the-meter, waterless advanced nuclear systems could support future AI factories,” John Josephakis, a global vice president at Nvidia, told Reuters.",
    "Utah spent the spring arguing over Kevin O’Leary’s Stratos data center project in Box Elder County, with public pushback centered on the Great Salt Lake, and Governor Spencer Cox responded with an executive order putting guardrails on data center development."
   ],
   "A2": [
    "On stage at the San Rafael Energy Lab outside Orangeville, a Valar team member plugged an Nvidia Spark desktop unit, running the company’s Blackwell architecture, into a circuit fed from the reactor hall.",
    "Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”",
    "“Through this work with Valar Atomics, Nvidia is exploring how behind-the-meter, waterless advanced nuclear systems could support future AI factories,” John Josephakis, a global vice president at Nvidia, told Reuters."
   ],
   "A3": [
    "Valar Atomics wired a Blackwell -based Nvidia desktop unit to its Ward 250 microreactor, served a website off the electricity, and announced a plan for something much bigger that skips the local water entirely.",
    "Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”",
    "“Through this work with Valar Atomics, Nvidia is exploring how behind-the-meter, waterless advanced nuclear systems could support future AI factories,” John Josephakis, a global vice president at Nvidia, told Reuters."
   ],
   "B1": [
    "More than 75 of these projects, worth around $130 billion, have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom’s Hardware ."
   ],
   "B2": [
