 E99 DeepSeek is developing its own AI chips to reduce its reliance on products from Nvidia and Huawei {"who": "DeepSeek", "what": "developing its own inference chips to cut reliance on NVIDIA and Huawei; early stage; talks with chip designers, foundries and memory suppliers; discreet hiring", "status": "rumour"}
A1 ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", 'Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\nDeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.', "Amid US restrictions on AI chip exports to China, Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", 'In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors.', "The launch also drove a surge in demand for Huawei's Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies.", 'OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.']
A2 ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "Amid US restrictions on AI chip exports to China, Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion."]
A3 ["According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\nDeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.", "Globally, DeepSeek's move follows a broader trend among major AI companies developing their own chips. OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.", "Amid US restrictions on AI chip exports to China, Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion."]
B1 ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "Amid US restrictions on AI chip exports to China, Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", 'In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors.', "The launch also drove a surge in demand for Huawei's Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies.", 'OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom', 'while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.', '"Nvidia\'s position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology," said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.', 'At the same time, DeepSeek has begun opening itself to external funding. Reuters previously reported that the company was preparing its first funding round worth US$7 billion, with a valuation of between US$52 billion and US$59 billion, ending a years-long strategy of rejecting outside investment.']
B3 ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", 'If successful, the company would join a number of global AI developers that have begun designing their own chips to gain greater control over computing infrastructure while reducing dependence on Nvidia.', '"Nvidia\'s position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology," said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.', "Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", "According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.", 'DeepSeek founder Liang Wenfeng acknowledged in a 2024 interview that chip export restrictions posed a challenge for the company.', "The base model supporting DeepSeek R1 was trained using Nvidia's H800 chips, a product specifically designed for the Chinese market before the US government banned its export in late 2023.", "In recent months, the company has increasingly relied on Huawei's ecosystem. In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors."]

